  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) This study investigates and evaluates whether densely filled, subwavelength 3D atomic arrays can use cooperative dipole interactions to create transverse Bloch-band resonances whose in-plane group velocities oppose their quasimomenta, thereby enabling high-transmission, robust negative refraction of light and an effective negative index without relying on artificial resonators.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
